WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
When two people care for the same pets, an
old plan can miss a new concern.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.280
Denlumi gives them one current record,
with clear reports and handovers.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.240
You're watching a fictional Alexa-style
browser demo.

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.060
These sample protocols have no
professional approval.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.260
There is no native Alexa connection.

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.260
Finn is the newcomer dog.

7
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.080
Nora is the resident cat.

8
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.080
The owner reviews this sample plan,

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.840
and both caregivers acknowledge the same
handover.

10
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.620
Before a person starts the software
session, the server checks the household,

11
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.180
current plan and protocol.

12
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.160
A report keeps who observed what, which
animal acted, the target,

13
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.400
uncertainty and timing.

14
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.860
The assistant drafts it.

15
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.380
A person confirms it.

16
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.760
The update pauses guidance and invalidates
older work.

17
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.600
Sam's old view is refused.

18
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.720
A new conversation gets the current record
through real,

19
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.220
authenticated HTTP MCP calls.

20
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.720
This answer uses a database template;
Bedrock inference is still blocked.

21
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.360
The report stays in history.

22
00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.680
The owner can preview a factual handover
privately.

23
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.920
Nothing is sent automatically.

24
00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.940
Stop works offline on this device.

25
00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.600
Its shared update waits for a connection.

26
00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.080
It stops software, without physically
stopping or supervising animals.

27
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.967
Each pairing has its own context: cat-cat,
dog-dog,

28
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.120
and either mixed newcomer.

29
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.360
Single-pet care needs no second pet.

30
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.440
Three-pet coordination does not authorize
group sessions.

31
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.260
This working demo uses local Supabase.

32
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.540
Earlier speech-provider checks used
synthetic input.

33
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.840
Human usability and qualified practical
review remain open.

34
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.140
Denlumi helps people coordinate; animal
outcomes have not been proven.
